# Installed dependencies. The plugin itself has none — every script runs on the Node the user
# already has, because a plugin that needs `npm install` to enforce its safety invariants does not
# enforce them on first run. This entry exists so that an incidental `npm install` cannot commit a
# tree of packages the plugin does not use.
node_modules/

# Nothing else belongs here. In particular:
#
#   docs/ is tracked on purpose. `validation-ledger.md` is the project's primary evidence — every
#   load-bearing claim with its verification method and verdict, including the ones that turned out
#   to be wrong — and `cost-model.md` now carries the only measurements anyone has taken. A README
#   that says "nothing here is assumed" and a repository that does not carry the proof would be a
#   worse combination than having no ledger at all.
#
#   Run data never appears here either, so it needs no rule: it lives under $CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA
#   (spec §20), which is what keeps the reviewer looking at your diff instead of our logs.
